      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **800 mg by mouth, three times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day, a common upper-range regimen.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours.** This is the standard regimen for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day.** This could be a typo for a daily total, split into doses.\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
